::scene INTRODUCTION

ROOM studio_stage

CAM 1 WIDE

SHOT

The broadcast opens on a brightly lit studio bathed in neon blues and warm amber lights. A packed audience applauds enthusiastically while the Tonight Show band finishes the opening bars of the theme.

SHOT_END

NPC npc_graham_mercer
NPC npc_john_akerson

announcer:
From somewhere above the smog and only slightly outside the blast radius...

ANNOUNCER:
It's...

ANNOUNCER:
The Tonight Show!

EVENT APPLAUSE

ANNOUNCER:
Tonight...

ANNOUNCER:
Corporate executives explain why exploding vending machines are actually a premium feature.

ANNOUNCER:
A local street chef prepares authentic mutant squid tacos.

ANNOUNCER:
And we'll meet a man who's legally declared his apartment to be an independent nation.

ANNOUNCER:
Ladies and gentlemen...

ANNOUNCER:
JOOOOOHN AKERSON!

EVENT APPLAUSE

ENTER john_akerson

CAM 2 TRACK john_akerson

SHOT

The camera follows John Akerson as he jogs onto the stage, shaking hands with audience members before stopping behind his desk with a broad smile.

SHOT_END

ACTION john_akerson waves to the crowd.

::scene MONOLOGUE

CAM 3 CLOSEUP john_akerson

JOHN:
Thank you!

JOHN:
Thank you!

JOHN:
Sit down! We've got a fantastic show tonight!

EVENT APPLAUSE

JOHN:
Did everyone survive the commute?

JOHN:
Traffic was backed up six blocks after somebody hacked the crossing lights to advertise noodles.

EVENT LAUGHTER

JOHN:
Corporate Security says crime is down.

JOHN:
Apparently they stopped counting anything outside corporate property.

EVENT LAUGHTER

JOHN:
I stopped by a pharmacy today.

JOHN:
They've started locking up bottled water.

JOHN:
The cybernetic organs are still self-service though.

EVENT LAUGHTER

JOHN:
You know times are tough when the mugger accepts store credit.

EVENT APPLAUSE

EVENT LAUGHTER

JOHN:
Good news though...

JOHN:
My landlord says the building is structurally sound.

JOHN:
Apparently that's a completely different thing than "safe."

EVENT LAUGHTER

